---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseStudyHeader from '../../components/notebook/CaseStudyHeader.astro';
import CaseHero from '../../components/notebook/CaseHero.astro';
import SectionRow from '../../components/notebook/SectionRow.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/notebook/Figure.astro';

import cover from '../../assets/depop-pop-ups/cover.png';
import features from '../../assets/depop-pop-ups/features.png';
import flowSignup from '../../assets/depop-pop-ups/flow-signup.png';
import flowNav from '../../assets/depop-pop-ups/flow-navigation.png';

/*
 * Team: Jonathan Gong, Tate Suarez, Varrshitha Kumar.
 * Context: BTG Product Management Academy at CMU, Spring 2026.
 * Presented to PNC leaders, CMU Tepper faculty, and the PMA cohort.
 */
---

<Base title="Depop Pop-Ups · VK">
  <div style="background: var(--paper); min-height: 100vh; color: var(--ink); padding-bottom: 120px">

    <CaseStudyHeader entryNum="" />

    <CaseHero
      eyebrow="Depop · BTG Product Management Academy"
      title="The real risk wasn't pop-ups cannibalizing the app"
      lede="A product strategy pitch for Depop: bring the in-person thrifting experience into the app through physical pop-ups, using an existing partnership, with all transactions staying on-platform."
      meta={[
        { label: "Role", value: "App mockups, trade-offs and risks, success metrics" },
        { label: "Team", value: "Jonathan Gong, Tate Suarez, Varrshitha Kumar" },
        { label: "Context", value: "BTG Product Management Academy at CMU, Spring 2026" },
        { label: "Audience", value: "PNC leaders, CMU Tepper faculty" },
      ]}
      cover={cover}
      coverAlt="Depop Pop-Ups presentation title slide with market photos and team names."
      note="handed: pitch a product strategy for Depop.<br><br>turned out: the real risk was sales leaving the app, not pop-ups replacing it."
    />

    <SectionRow num="01" label="the gap">
      <Fragment slot="main">
        <p class="body">
          Half of U.S. consumers still prefer to buy secondhand in person. The feeling of the
          fabric, the unexpected find, the social experience of going with a friend — none of that
          exists in an infinite scroll. Depop already had an asset that pointed at a solution:
          a partnership with SOOK UK, which runs physical vintage markets. The connection between
          that partnership and the Depop app wasn't built. We built it.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="margin">
        <p class="note" style="margin:0;transform:rotate(-1deg)">
          building on what already exists instead of inventing something new was the strategic
          move. a new physical market business from scratch is a different pitch.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    </SectionRow>

    <SectionRow num="02" label="three features">
      <Fragment slot="main">
        <p class="body">
          Depop Pop-Ups adds three things to the app. A discovery page surfaces nearby pop-up
          events matched to your clothing interests, so you find out about a market the same way
          you find a listing. An interactive map shows the event live, with vendor information
          cards, inventory, ratings, and price range, navigable by GPS. A digital passport collects
          a stamp for every pop-up attended, turning a one-time visit into something social and
          collectible.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          My role was the app mockups, the trade-offs and risks section, and the success metrics.
          The mockups were designed with AI tools but grounded in real Depop UI patterns so the
          features read as part of the existing app, not a separate one.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    </SectionRow>

    <Figure
      fig="fig. 1"
      wide
      caption="Feature overview: Discovery page, interactive pop-up map with seller info cards and vendor filtering, and digital passport with collectible stamps."
      images={[
        { src: features, alt: "Three-column slide: Discovery Page (find pop-ups near you or by interest), Interactive Pop-up Map (live event map with seller cards, GPS, vendor filtering), Digital Passport Card (collect a stamp for every pop-up attended)." },
      ]}
    />

    <SectionRow num="03" label="the question that mattered">
      <Fragment slot="main">
        <p class="body">
          The first question from the PNC leaders in the Q&A wasn't about the features. It was
          about where the money goes. Physical markets invite cash. Cash sales would take
          transactions off Depop entirely — no revenue, no reviews, no data.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          Our answer: all pop-up purchases go through the Depop app, discouraging cash and keeping
          every sale tied to a seller profile. The event becomes a channel that feeds the platform
          rather than a competitor. The second concern raised was whether we were converting
          online shoppers into offline ones. Our position was that the audiences are largely
          distinct, and that in-app purchases and reviews after a pop-up keep attendees engaged
          online. The honest answer is that the first rollout would need to test that claim directly.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="margin">
        <p class="note" style="margin:0;transform:rotate(0.8deg)">
          i'd design the metrics around the riskiest assumption from the start next time, not after
          the Q&A. the cannibalization question was predictable.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    </SectionRow>

    <Figure
      fig="fig. 2"
      caption="User flows: sign-up (discover → event details → RSVP) and navigation (collect stamp → live vendor map → post-purchase review)."
      note="the passport stamp comes before the map, not after. you commit to the event, then navigate it."
      images={[
        { src: flowSignup, alt: "Sign-up flow: Pop-up Discovery Page showing nearby events on map, Pop-up Event Details with seller list and schedule, RSVP Confirmation screen.", label: "sign-up flow" },
        { src: flowNav, alt: "Navigation flow: Collect Pop-up Passport Stamp screen, Live Vendor Map with active vendors and GPS navigation, Post-Purchase Review screen.", label: "navigation flow" },
      ]}
    />

    <footer class="cs-row" style="padding-top: 24px; align-items: end">
      <div></div>
      <a href="/projects" class="back mono">← Projects</a>
      <div></div>
    </footer>

  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .body {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.62;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 20, 'wght' 400;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .body:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .back { color: var(--ink-60); text-decoration: none; font-size: 13px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .body { font-size: 19px; } }
</style>
